build: 2026-06-28 v10.76.41 (Fix: selection menus freeze while playing)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notesT: Builds on 10.76.40. Fixes the recurring "you suddenly can't select the Tonart/
  Genre anymore" freeze. Root cause: the main screen was reading the camera pulse status
  (finger-on-lens + the live acquisition readout), which updates ~10×/s while a take plays.
  Reading those on the MAIN view meant SwiftUI rebuilt the WHOLE screen ten times a second
  — and every rebuild closed any dropdown menu you had just opened, so a tap couldn't land.
  No crash, just an un-selectable menu (worse while playing — exactly when those readings
  tick). Fix: moved both fast-updating readouts into their own small sub-views (the bio
  strip and a new pulse-readout view), so only those tiny views refresh 10×/s while the
  selection menus' screen stays still. No new sheets, no structural change to the modal
  chain — can't reintroduce the black-screen crash. ui-state-reviewer + build-error-resolver:
  GO.
  Test: 10.76.41 → start a take (Create from Within), put a finger on the camera, then open
  Compose ▸ Composition ▸ Tonart / Genre / Tone-system dropdown — it should stay open and
  let you pick, no freeze, while playing. Still launches straight to Studio.
